{{head|lad|determiners|first-person singular possessive singular||plural|mis|g=s|Hebrew spelling|מי}}<ref name="Folkmasa">{{R:lad:Folkmasa}}</ref>

# {{lb|lad|before the noun}} {{apocopic form of|lad|mío}}, [[my]]
#* {{quote-web|lad|author=Alicia Sisso Raz|title=Unas membranzas de momentos pascuales|url=http://www.vocesdehaketia.com/novedades/Pesah.pdf|text=En '''mi''' corassón están grabadas con muncho cariño unos recuerdos endiamantados de la pascua enca de mis padres, ya ḥasrá.|t=Advantageous memories of '''my''' parents’ home Seder are kept so dearly in my heart; those were the days.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The forms {{m|lad|mi}} and {{m|lad|mis}} are only used before and within the [[noun phrase]] of the modified noun. In other positions, a form of {{m|lad|mío}} is used instead.
: {{ux|lad|Son '''mis''' livros.|inline=1|They are my books.}}
: {{ux|lad|Los livros son '''míos'''.|inline=1|The books are mine.}}

Besides being a pronoun, because '''''mi''''' occurs in a noun phrase and expresses reference, it also grammatically classifies as a {{glossary|determiner}} (specifically a possessive/genitive determiner).

