==Spanish==

===Pronunciation===
{{es-pr}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|es|la|meus}}, when it was eliding before a vowel-initial word in speech.

====Determiner====
{{head|es|determiners|first-person singular possessive singular||plural|mis|g=s}}

# {{lb|es|before the noun}} {{apocopic form of|es|mío}}, [[my]]

=====Usage notes=====
* The forms {{m|es|mi}} and {{m|es|mis}} are only used before and within the [[noun phrase]] of the modified noun. In other positions, a form of {{m|es|mío}} is used instead.
: {{ux|es|Son '''mis''' libros.|inline=1|They are my books.}}
: {{ux|es|Los libros son '''míos'''.|inline=1|The books are mine.}}

Besides being a pronoun, because '''''mi''''' occurs in a noun phrase and expresses reference, it also grammatically classifies as a {{glossary|determiner}} (specifically a possessive/genitive determiner).

